  "what_changed": "Introduces a `dispatch_validated()` wrapper at the LLM-to-typed-code boundary in `scripts/orchestrator_runner.py` and `scripts/verify_runner.py`, wired into 8 of the 9 subagent call sites. Off-contract LLM responses now surface as specific `schema_invalid: <name>: <field-detail>` reasons in `state.current_run.partial_reasons` instead of being silently swallowed by `dict.get()` fallbacks (the v0.1.1 Mode-B silent-no-op bug). All 7 agent `.md` files gain an authoritative `## Output schema (canonical)` section embedding the JSON Schema and a \"Return ONLY a JSON object\" instruction. Two new test suites are added: a parameterized drift-prevention lint (7 cases asserting `.md` schema blocks stay JSON-equivalent to `agents/schemas/*.schema.json`) and an end-to-end soft-fail integration test reproducing the observed wrong shape and asserting the specific reason surfaces. Test count grows from 146 to 158 with no new runtime dependencies.",
  "why": "The v0.1.1 orchestrator silently accepted malformed subagent responses — any off-schema field was absorbed by `dict.get()` defaults, causing the pipeline to continue with phantom data and no diagnostic signal (Mode-B bug). CCE-4 hardens the LLM boundary so schema violations are explicit, attributable, and surfaced in the partial-run record rather than hidden. Embedding the schema directly in each agent's system prompt makes the contract self-documenting and reduces prompt/code drift.",
